<title>HUNGARY: BUDAPEST BOURSE PUBLISHES 1997 HOLIDAY TIMETABLE.</title>
<headline>BUDAPEST BOURSE PUBLISHES 1997 HOLIDAY TIMETABLE.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Budapest Stock Exchange (BSE) announced its timetable for the days when it will be closed in the next eleven months.</p>
<p>The holidays are the following:</p>
<p>    1997  March 31 (Monday)	 -   Easter</p>
<p>	    May 1 (Thursday)	  -   Labour Day</p>
<p>	    May 2 (Friday)</p>
<p>	    May 19 (Monday)	   -   Whitsun</p>
<p>	    August 20 (Wednesday)   -   King Saint Stephen's Day</p>
<p>	    October 23 (Thursday)   -   National holiday</p>
<p>	    October 24 (Friday)</p>
<p>	    December 24, 25, 26     -   Christmas</p>
<p>	    December 31 (Wednesday)</p>
<p>    1998  January 1 (Thursday)    -   New year's Day</p>
<p>	    January 2 (Friday)</p>
<p>	    January 5 (Monday</p>
<p>	    January 6 (Tuesday)</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
